## 2. Duties after receipt {#bast-duties}

1. The Client changes every password meant for people (Annex 2) within {{ (pw_days ~ " (" ~ (pw_days | words) ~ ") days") if pw_days else NP }} of the date of this certificate, as described in chapter 6 and Appendix E of the technical documentation, and changes the passphrase of the credentials file. The Client keeps the credentials file as the record of the accounts.
2. On {{ d(a.get("vendor_access_end")) }}, the Provider's SSH key and internet addresses are removed from the servers and the allow-lists.
{% if state_owner == "vendor" %}
3. The Provider keeps the installer's records (ansibro's state/ folder), which are needed to change the system later. When the Client changes a password of the kind that the installer also uses, the Client sends the new value back to the Provider in a re-encrypted credentials file; otherwise the next install undoes the change or fails. The Client also has a copy of these records in the credentials file, so it can change provider at any time.
{% else %}
3. The Client keeps the installer's records (ansibro's state/ folder), from the credentials file, group "{{ groups.internal[first_lang] }}". The Provider deletes its own copy when the parties agree.
{% endif %}

